'''Systems chemistry''' is the science of studying [[Network science|networks]] of interacting molecules, to create new functions from a set (or library) of molecules with different hierarchical levels and emergent properties.<ref>{{cite book|last1= Sadownik |last2=Otto |title=Encyclopedia of Astrobiology |chapter=Systems Chemistry |date=2014 | pages = 1–3 |doi=10.1007/978-3-642-27833-4_1095-2 |isbn=978-3-642-27833-4 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.rug.nl/research/centre-systems-chemistry/|title=Centre for Systems Chemistry|website=University of Groningen|date=27 October 2011|accessdate=26 October 2017}}</ref>

Systems chemistry is also related to the origin of life ([[abiogenesis]]).<ref>{{cite journal|last1= Kiedrowski|last2=Otto|last3=Herdewijn |year= 2010| title = Welcome Home, Systems Chemists! | journal = Journal of Systems Chemistry |volume = 1| pages = 1 |doi=10.1186/1759-2208-1-1 |doi-access= free |hdl= 11370/28ddfb30-005b-4724-b67b-0ce7a4f07136 |hdl-access= free }}</ref>

